{
  "id": "Compound::DB00761 - Gene::9990",
  "verbalization": "Potassium Chloride appears to interact with Slc12a6 through a series of molecular and functional pathways that involve cationic transport and symport activity. The evidence suggests that Potassium Chloride binds to Slc12a5 and Slc12a7, which are both involved in cation-coupled chloride transport and potassium-ion symport mechanisms. These transporters are ultimately participated by Slc12a6, indicating a potential functional link between these proteins. The overlapping roles of Slc12a5 and Slc12a7 in facilitating chloride transport, combined with their participation in symport activity, suggest that Potassium Chloride may influence Slc12a6 through a shared functional mechanism. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of these transporters in maintaining ion homeostasis, and the involvement of Potassium Chloride in their regulation may be critical for their function.",
